# 2. Users and Authorization Module

## Module description

This module manages the users who operate the POS system.

The system initially supports two roles:

* `admin`
* `employee`

Administrators have complete access to the system.

Employees receive permissions based on their role and optional per-user permission overrides.

Every important action performed by a user must be recorded in an audit log.

Users may work in one or multiple stores.

---

## 2.1 Table: `roles`

### Description

Stores system roles.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
code                VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL
description         VARCHAR(255) NULL
is_system           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Initial records

```text
admin
employee
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(code)
```

---

## 2.2 Table: `permissions`

### Description

Stores individual actions that can be granted to roles or users.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
code                VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
module              VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
description         VARCHAR(255) NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Example permission codes

```text
users.view
users.create
users.update
users.delete
users.permissions.manage

stores.view
stores.manage

products.view
products.create
products.update
products.delete
products.prices.manage

inventory.view
inventory.adjust
inventory.transfer
inventory.receive

sales.create
sales.discount
sales.void
sales.refund

