UNIQUE(code)
INDEX(module)
```

---

## 2.3 Table: `users`

### Description

Stores POS operators and administrators.

Users belong to a business and may be assigned to multiple stores.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
business_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
role_id             BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
code                CHAR(6) NOT NULL
first_name          VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL
last_name           VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL
email               VARCHAR(254) NULL
phone               VARCHAR(20) NULL
avatar_path         VARCHAR(255) NULL
password            VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
pin_hash            VARCHAR(255) NULL
status              VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'
email_verified_at   TIMESTAMP NULL
last_login_at       TIMESTAMP NULL
remember_token      VARCHAR(100) NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
deleted_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
business_id -> businesses.id
role_id -> roles.id
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(business_id, code)
UNIQUE(business_id, email)
INDEX(role_id, status)
INDEX(business_id, status)
INDEX(business_id, last_name, first_name)
```

### Business rules

* Generate `code` automatically.
* The code must contain exactly six characters.
* Never store the POS PIN directly.
* Hash the PIN using Laravel's password hashing system.
* Email may be null.
* Soft-deleted users must remain referenced by historical transactions.
* User status may include:

```text
active
inactive
suspended
```

---

## 2.4 Table: `permission_role`

### Description

