```

### Example action values

```text
user.login
user.logout
user.created
user.updated
user.permission_changed

product.created
product.updated
product.deleted
product.price_changed

sale.created
sale.completed
sale.voided
sale.refunded

inventory.adjusted
inventory.transferred
inventory.received

shift.opened
shift.closed

settings.updated
```

### Indexes

```text
INDEX(user_id, created_at)
INDEX(store_id, created_at)
INDEX(terminal_id, created_at)
INDEX(auditable_type, auditable_id, created_at)
INDEX(action, created_at)
INDEX(request_uuid)
```

### Business rules

* Audit logs must not be physically updated after creation.
* Use `nullOnDelete()` for user, store, and terminal references.
* Record both old and new values when data is modified.
* Sensitive values such as passwords and authentication tokens must never be recorded.

