# 3. Business and Stores Module

## Module description

This module stores the main business information, its stores, assigned users, and POS terminals.

A business may own multiple stores.

Each store may contain multiple POS terminals or computers.

Products belong to a shared business catalog, while inventory quantities and costs are maintained independently by store.

---

## 3.1 Table: `business_categories`

### Description

Stores configurable business categories.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
code                VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Example values

```text
grocery
convenience_store
pharmacy
restaurant
hardware_store
clothing_store
other
```

### Constraints

```text
UNIQUE(code)
UNIQUE(name)
```

---

## 3.2 Table: `businesses`

### Description

Stores the legal and commercial information of the business operating the POS.

This replaces the original `store_info` table because the information belongs to the business, not to a single store.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
category_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
name                VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
legal_name          VARCHAR(160) NOT NULL
tax_id              VARCHAR(30) NULL
bio                 VARCHAR(500) NULL
