INDEX(name)
INDEX(tax_id)
```

---

## 3.3 Table: `stores`

### Description

Stores each physical business location.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
business_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
manager_user_id     BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
code                VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
phone_line_1        VARCHAR(20) NULL
phone_line_2        VARCHAR(20) NULL
email               VARCHAR(254) NULL
address_line_1      VARCHAR(160) NOT NULL
address_line_2      VARCHAR(160) NULL
neighborhood        VARCHAR(100) NULL
city                VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
state               VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
postal_code         VARCHAR(12) NOT NULL
country_code        CHAR(2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'MX'
timezone            VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'America/Mexico_City'
is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
deleted_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
business_id -> businesses.id
manager_user_id -> users.id
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(business_id, code)
INDEX(business_id, is_active)
INDEX(manager_user_id)
INDEX(city, state)
```

### Business rules

* Postal codes must use strings, not numeric fields.
* A store manager must belong to the same business.
* A store manager should also have a corresponding `store_user` assignment.
* Use `nullOnDelete()` for `manager_user_id`.

---

## 3.4 Table: `store_user`

### Description

Associates users with the stores where they are authorized to work.

### Columns

```text
store_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
user_id             BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
is_default          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE
is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE
job_title           VARCHAR(80) NULL
assigned_at         TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
store_id -> stores.id
user_id -> users.id
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
PRIMARY KEY(store_id, user_id)
INDEX(user_id, is_active)
INDEX(store_id, is_active)
```

### Business rules

* A user may work in multiple stores.
* A user should have no more than one default store.
* The single-default-store rule must be validated in the application.

---

## 3.5 Table: `pos_terminals`

### Description

Represents each POS terminal, computer, or device installed in a store.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
store_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
code                VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL
device_uuid         CHAR(36) NULL
printer_name        VARCHAR(120) NULL
app_version         VARCHAR(30) NULL
last_seen_at        TIMESTAMP NULL
is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE
metadata            JSON NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
deleted_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
