# 8. Product Pricing and Discount Rules Module

## Module description

This module manages product prices and quantity-based discounts.

Products may have up to three initial price lists:

* Menudeo
* Mayoreo
* Caja

The architecture must not limit the system to exactly three price types.

Administrators must be able to add more price lists later.

Prices may be:

* Global for the business
* Specific to a store
* Valid only during a date range

---

## 8.1 Table: `price_lists`

### Description

Defines named pricing groups.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
business_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
store_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
code                VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL
name                VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL
currency_code       CHAR(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'MXN'
priority            SMALLINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL DEFAULT 100
is_default          BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE
is_active           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
deleted_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
business_id -> businesses.id
store_id -> stores.id
```

### Initial records

```text
retail       Menudeo
wholesale    Mayoreo
box          Caja
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(business_id, store_id, code)
INDEX(store_id, is_active, priority)
INDEX(business_id, is_active, priority)
```

### Business rules

MySQL permits multiple null values inside unique indexes.

Therefore, application validation must prevent duplicate business-wide codes when `store_id` is null.

Only one default price list should exist per effective scope.

---

## 8.2 Table: `product_prices`

### Description

Stores prices assigned to products through price lists.

### Columns

```text
id                      BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
product_id              BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
price_list_id           BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
price                   DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL
valid_from              TIMESTAMP NULL
valid_until             TIMESTAMP NULL
created_by_user_id      BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
created_at              TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at              TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
product_id -> products.id
price_list_id -> price_lists.id
created_by_user_id -> users.id
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(product_id, price_list_id, valid_from)
INDEX(price_list_id, product_id)
INDEX(product_id, valid_from, valid_until)
```

### Business rules

* Price validity periods must not overlap for the same product and price list.
* Overlap validation must be implemented in the application service.
* Price changes must be recorded in `audit_logs`.
* Historical sales retain their own price snapshot.

---

## 8.3 Table: `product_quantity_rules`

### Description

Stores quantity-based pricing and discount rules.

It supports requirements such as:

* Buy at least 10 products and use the wholesale price.
* Buy at least 12 products and use the box price.
* Buy 3 products and receive a fixed discount.
* For every 3 products, receive a repeated fixed discount.
* Buy at least 5 products and receive a percentage discount.

### Columns

```text
id                      BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
product_id              BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
price_list_id           BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
name                    VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
rule_type               VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL
minimum_quantity        DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
group_quantity          DECIMAL(14,4) NULL
discount_value          DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL
repeatable              BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE
priority                SMALLINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL DEFAULT 100
starts_at               TIMESTAMP NULL
ends_at                 TIMESTAMP NULL
is_active               BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE
created_by_user_id      BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
created_at              TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at              TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
product_id -> products.id
price_list_id -> price_lists.id
created_by_user_id -> users.id
```

### Allowed rule types

```text
fixed_unit_price
percentage_discount
fixed_line_discount
fixed_group_discount
```

### Example

For every three products, apply a $5 discount:

```text
rule_type          = fixed_group_discount
minimum_quantity   = 3
group_quantity     = 3
discount_value     = 5.0000
repeatable         = true
```

For ten or more products, use a unit price of $15:

```text
rule_type          = fixed_unit_price
minimum_quantity   = 10
group_quantity     = null
discount_value     = 15.0000
repeatable         = false
```

### Indexes

```text
INDEX(product_id, is_active, starts_at, ends_at)
INDEX(price_list_id, product_id)
INDEX(product_id, minimum_quantity, priority)
```

### Business rules

* Higher-priority rules must be evaluated first.
* The application must define whether multiple rules may stack.
* The selected rule and calculated discount must be copied to the sale item discount records.
* Historical sales must not recalculate old discounts from current rules.

