created_at                 TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at                 TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
store_id -> stores.id
product_id -> products.id
preferred_supplier_id -> suppliers.id
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
PRIMARY KEY(store_id, product_id)
INDEX(product_id, is_available)
INDEX(store_id, is_available)
INDEX(preferred_supplier_id)
```

---

## 10.2 Table: `inventory_balances`

### Description

Stores the current inventory balance for each product and store.

This table is optimized for fast inventory lookups.

### Columns

```text
store_id               BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
product_id             BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
quantity_on_hand       DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
quantity_reserved      DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
version                BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
updated_at             TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
store_id -> stores.id
product_id -> products.id
```

### Constraints

```text
PRIMARY KEY(store_id, product_id)
```

### Calculated value

```text
quantity_available =
    quantity_on_hand - quantity_reserved
```

### Business rules

* Update balances only inside database transactions.
* Use row locking when posting inventory movements.
* Increment `version` during each inventory update.
* Do not use this table as the only inventory history.

---

## 10.3 Table: `inventory_movements`

### Description

Stores an immutable inventory ledger.

Every stock increase or decrease must generate an inventory movement.

### Columns

```text
id                  BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
uuid                CHAR(36) NOT NULL
store_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
product_id          BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
user_id             BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
shift_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
movement_type       VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL
quantity            DECIMAL(14,4) NOT NULL
unit_cost           DECIMAL(14,4) NULL
balance_after       DECIMAL(14,4) NULL
reference_type      VARCHAR(80) NULL
reference_id        BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
reason              VARCHAR(255) NULL
occurred_at         TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
created_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
store_id -> stores.id
product_id -> products.id
user_id -> users.id
shift_id -> cash_shifts.id
```

### Allowed movement types

```text
opening
purchase_receipt
sale
sale_return
transfer_out
transfer_in
adjustment_in
adjustment_out
stock_count
waste
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(uuid)
INDEX(store_id, product_id, occurred_at)
INDEX(product_id, occurred_at)
INDEX(reference_type, reference_id)
INDEX(user_id, occurred_at)
INDEX(movement_type, occurred_at)
```

### Business rules

* Inventory movements must not be updated after creation.
* Corrections must use a reversing movement.
* Positive quantities represent stock increases.
* Negative quantities represent stock decreases.
* For sales, use negative quantities.
* For purchase receipts, use positive quantities.

