# 11. Store Transfers Module

## Module description

This module transfers inventory from one store to another.

A transfer should produce:

* A `transfer_out` movement at the source store
* A `transfer_in` movement at the destination store

The inventory must not simply be changed without ledger movements.

---

## 11.1 Table: `stock_transfers`

### Description

Stores the transfer header and workflow state.

### Columns

```text
id                          BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT
uuid                        CHAR(36) NOT NULL
transfer_number             VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL
source_store_id             BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
destination_store_id        BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
status                      VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'draft'
requested_by_user_id        BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL
approved_by_user_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
shipped_by_user_id          BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
received_by_user_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NULL
requested_at                TIMESTAMP NULL
approved_at                 TIMESTAMP NULL
shipped_at                  TIMESTAMP NULL
received_at                 TIMESTAMP NULL
cancelled_at                TIMESTAMP NULL
notes                       TEXT NULL
created_at                  TIMESTAMP NULL
updated_at                  TIMESTAMP NULL
```

### Relationships

```text
source_store_id -> stores.id
destination_store_id -> stores.id
requested_by_user_id -> users.id
approved_by_user_id -> users.id
shipped_by_user_id -> users.id
received_by_user_id -> users.id
```

### Allowed statuses

```text
draft
requested
approved
in_transit
partially_received
received
cancelled
```

### Constraints and indexes

```text
UNIQUE(uuid)
UNIQUE(source_store_id, transfer_number)
INDEX(source_store_id, status, created_at)
INDEX(destination_store_id, status, created_at)
```

### Business rules

```text
source_store_id != destination_store_id
```

* Source and destination stores must belong to the same business.
* Inventory should be deducted when the transfer is shipped.
* Destination inventory should be increased when the transfer is received.
* A partially received transfer must track shipped and received quantities independently.

